On Sat, 10 Oct 2026 10:21:15 -0700, Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com> wrote:
> Add a just process-email task. It deterministically iterates over each
> of the emails tagged with inbox and runs `claude --permission-mode auto
> -p "/process-email"` on them one at a time.
>
> If there are no more inbox messages found, the loop ends.

Done in "[PATCH 0/3] Add just process-email" [1]. The recipe is in the
trunk Justfile, alongside the skill it runs. Each pass is a fresh
`claude --permission-mode auto -p "/process-email <id>"` with its output
sent to /dev/null. The loop ends when the inbox is empty. After each
pass it re-indexes and checks that the message has left the inbox. If
the message is still there, the loop stops with an error instead of
running claude on it again and again.

> The skill needs to be updated to take a
> message id as an argument.

/process-email now takes an optional `id:<message-id>`. If that
message is no longer in the inbox, the pass stops without writing
anything.

> Perhaps
> there's a `just get-oldest-inbox-message` task that does that, that
> `just process-email` and /process-email can both reference? I'd like to
> keep that logic in one place. I think it's probably for useful for
> /process-email to work without args, in which case it should look it up
> using the same tool as `just process-email`.

Agreed, and that's how it works. `just get-oldest-inbox-message`
holds the only copy of the query. The loop calls it, and so does the
skill when it is given no argument.

One gap is left, and I'd like your call on it. The loop doesn't fetch.
It walks the inbox as currently indexed, and the passes themselves pull
in new mail. If the local index is empty at the start, the loop exits
without running claude, even when upstream has new mail. The fix I'd
suggest is to move the skill's "get up to date" step (fetch, rebase,
notmuch new) into its own recipe, which the loop runs before each
lookup and the skill calls as step 1. That keeps that logic in one
place too. Shall I send it as a follow-up?

The series edits step 2 of the skill, as two pending patches do,
"[PATCH] claude: Treat unintegrated mail as revisable drafts" [2] and
"[PATCH] claude: Update stale threads from process-email" [3].
Whichever lands second needs a small rebase.

